          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "उत्थानम् — utthānam — \"a rise\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "यदि देशस्य उत्थानं भवति, तर्हि जनाः प्रसन्नाः भविष्यन्ति। yadi deśasya utthānaṃ bhavati, tarhi janāḥ prasannāḥ bhaviṣyanti. If the country rises, the people will be glad."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A neuter noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "उत्थानम् (utthānam) is built on ud, \"up\", and the root √sthā, \"to stand\", which also gives uttiṣṭhati; MW gives utthāna as standing up, rising (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
